; Loss-free used_information P4: `force_int` walks a Peano spine whose
; inner thunk is branch-pruned to one world under pc = b; it must thread
; that used_information (= b) into `s`'s cache entry. Discarding it caches
; `used = true`: under b the nat is 1 (1 <= 1, True); the ~b branch then
; hits the stale entry and reports (not True) = False. Correct: under ~b
; the nat is 2 (2 <= 1 is False), so (not False) = True — a single
; True item at probability 1.
(query
 (let ((b (flip 0.5))
       (s (native_leq (S (if b (O) (S (O)))) @1)))
   (Posterior (if b s (not s)) True)))
